                                                    "desc:8":  "Steam leaves the silo through the 3x3 Spine duct the projection built east of the silo. Along its bore sit FOUR rotor sockets - in survival the auto-build blanks them with turbine casings, so swap in your four Turbine Housings, then RIGHT-CLICK each to set CLOCKWISE or ANTICLOCKWISE. Order matters: backwash swirl accumulates from housing to housing. A rotor spinning WITH the incoming swirl rides it for more steam speed (and more heat); one set AGAINST it cancels the swirl for more EU per litre. Same-direction trains are fast and thirsty, alternating trains are efficient and cool. There is no single right answer - only your goal.",
